// LateSlotActor — test fixture for BT-3548 (ADR 0124 §2/B2)
//
// A `late state:` field has no default and no `initialize` method assigning
// it, so its key must be entirely absent from init/1's state literal — not
// `nil` — until something explicitly assigns it. This exercises:
//   - the actor spawns without raising UninitializedStateError (B2 excludes
//     `late` slots from the post-initialize definite-assignment check)
//   - `sys:get_state/1` shows no `proc` key at all after a plain `spawn`
//   - `spawnWith: #{#proc => v}` (InitArgs merged over DefaultState) still
//     supplies the slot, showing it present in state afterward
//
// `getProc` is only called by tests once `proc` has been supplied via
// `spawnWith:` — reading an unassigned `late` slot is an unguarded
// `maps:get/2` until B3 ships the guarded read (out of scope here).

typed Actor subclass: LateSlotActor
  late state: proc :: Subprocess
  state: count :: Integer = 0

  getCount -> Integer => self.count

  getProc -> Subprocess => self.proc
